---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout current="practice" title="Tools: the real source of agent capability">
  <section class="section page-section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Agent capability</p>
      <h1>Tools: the real source of agent capability</h1>
      <p>
        A tool is any controlled interface that lets the model read fresh state
        or change the outside world. Different tool forms create different
        capability boundaries.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="tools-grid">
      <a class="tool-card is-featured" href="/function-tools/">
        <span class="tool-star" aria-label="Deep dive">*</span>
        <span class="tool-kind">Typed action</span>
        <h3>Function tools</h3>
        <p>
          Small, explicit functions with schemas. Best for narrow actions like
          creating a ticket, validating an order, or checking machine status.
        </p>
      </a>
      <article class="tool-card">
        <span class="tool-kind">Shared interface</span>
        <h3>MCP servers</h3>
        <p>
          External capability providers that expose tools, resources, and
          prompts. Useful when integrations need auth, state, or reuse across
          agents.
        </p>
      </article>
      <a class="tool-card is-featured" href="/skills/">
        <span class="tool-star" aria-label="Deep dive">*</span>
        <span class="tool-kind">Packaged procedure</span>
        <h3>Skills</h3>
        <p>
          Repeatable playbooks with instructions, scripts, templates, and
          examples. Good for domain workflows that need consistent execution.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a class="tool-card is-featured" href="/code-execution/">
        <span class="tool-star" aria-label="Deep dive">*</span>
        <span class="tool-kind">Runtime feedback</span>
        <h3>Code execution</h3>
        <p>
          A sandbox for calculating, transforming files, running tests, and
          inspecting repos. Powerful because observations are concrete.
        </p>
      </a>
      <article class="tool-card">
        <span class="tool-kind">Grounding</span>
        <h3>Search and retrieval</h3>
        <p>
          Web search, docs lookup, vector search, and database queries. These
          tools keep decisions tied to current or private information.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="tool-card">
        <span class="tool-kind">Control point</span>
        <h3>Human handoff</h3>
        <p>
          Approval, review, escalation, and override are tools too. They keep
          high-risk actions inside an inspectable operating model.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
